---
import LongForm from '../layouts/LongForm.astro';
import { homePicks, coverFor, fmtMonthYear } from '../lib/data';

const toc = [
  { slug: 'shape', text: 'The shape of me' },
  { slug: 'got-here', text: 'How I got here' },
  { slug: 'now', text: 'What I do now' },
  { slug: 'others', text: 'What people tell me' },
  { slug: 'care', text: 'What I care about' },
  { slug: 'clock', text: 'Off the clock' },
  { slug: 'head', text: "What's in my head" },
  { slug: 'next', text: "What's next" },
];

const notes = [
  { label: 'Based', text: 'Bangalore. From Ambala, grew up in Himachal.' },
  { label: 'Studied', text: 'B.Com (Hons), Delhi University. CFA Level 1 done, Level 2 next.' },
  { label: 'Work', text: 'Research at Zerodha. Helps Rainmatter with research.' },
  { label: 'Before', text: 'Content for PhonePe’s stockbroking arm.' },
  { label: 'In numbers', text: '500+ pieces · 100+ videos · 1000+ failures survived.' },
  { label: 'Built', text: 'FinanceRadar →', href: '/finance-radar/' },
  { label: 'Helps with', text: 'Money, one on one →', href: '/financial-planning/' },
];

const bar = ['Tech + Claude Code', 'Product', 'Content + social', 'Videos', 'Sport', 'Philosophy'];
const path = [
  { k: 'Ambala', b: 'Home', p: 'Son of an accountant and a commerce teacher.' },
  { k: 'Gr. 6–12', b: 'Boarding, Himachal', p: 'Topper, badminton, debating.' },
  { k: 'College', b: 'B.Com (Hons), DU', p: 'COVID, then markets.' },
  { k: 'Then', b: 'PhonePe', p: 'Stockbroking content.' },
  { k: 'Now', b: 'Zerodha', p: 'Research + Rainmatter.' },
];
const score = [
  { v: 'Nat’l', u: '', b: 'Badminton', p: 'National level in school. Still play.' },
  { v: '80', u: '', b: 'Cricket', p: 'Best Sunday-league knock.' },
  { v: '21', u: 'K', b: 'Running', p: 'Nandi Hills, untrained.' },
  { v: '~500', u: 'km', b: 'Biking', p: 'Longest ride so far.' },
];
---
<LongForm
  title="About"
  description="Kashish Kapoor: researcher at Zerodha, Rainmatter, FinanceRadar. How he got into finance, what he cares about, cricket, running and rabbit holes."
  kicker="About · the long version"
  heading="Finance geek. Experimenter."
  headingEm="Sporty human."
  lead="I do research at Zerodha, help Rainmatter think through its bets, and build things like FinanceRadar on the side. This is the long version: how I got here, what I care about, what I do when I'm not working, and what I'm figuring out next."
  toc={toc}
  notes={notes}
>
  <div slot="hero">
    <img class="ab-av" src="/images/avatar.jpg" alt="Cartoon portrait of Kashish Kapoor" width="600" height="600" fetchpriority="high" />
  </div>

  <section id="shape">
    <h2>The shape of me</h2>
    <p>If you asked me who I am, the honest answer is that I get interested in a lot of things. Finance is at the centre, but I've become more of a generalist: someone who can tinker across tech, product, content and finance, and go deep when something grabs me.</p>
    <p>The best way I've found to describe it is a <span class="hl">T-shaped person</span>. The top of the T is everything I'm curious about. The stem is where I've gone deep.</p>
    <figure class="tee" aria-label="T-shape diagram">
      <div class="tee-bar">{bar.map((b) => <span>{b}</span>)}</div>
      <div class="tee-stem">
        <span class="k">The deep bit</span>
        <b>Finance</b>
        <small>Banking · insurance · broking · wealth · payments</small>
        <b>Energy + climate</b>
        <small>Generation · transmission · new tech</small>
      </div>
    </figure>
    <p>I'm still figuring out which other things I want to be an expert at. That's half the fun.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="got-here">
    <h2>How I got here</h2>
    <ol class="path">
      {path.map((s) => <li><span class="k">{s.k}</span><b>{s.b}</b><small>{s.p}</small></li>)}
    </ol>
    <p>I'm from Ambala, but most of my good memories of growing up are from a boarding school in Himachal, where I lived from grade 6 to 12. I was the kid who was into everything: topping the class, national-level badminton, debating, business competitions.</p>
    <p>My headmaster wanted me to take engineering. He knew I was a bright kid, and that's the path bright kids were pushed down. I didn't want it. I picked commerce. With an accountant for a dad and a commerce teacher for a mum, maybe that was always coming.</p>
    <p>I tried accounting first and found it boring. I tried marketing too, and it didn't stick. Then COVID happened. Classes at Delhi University, where I was doing my B.Com (Hons), barely ran, and I found the stock market.</p>
    <blockquote>I knew I was really into it when I was spending sleepless nights reading finance books.</blockquote>
    <p>I did course after course and built financial models in my own time, for no reason other than wanting to understand how things worked. In college I was also on the placement cell and kept debating, but finance had me.</p>
    <p>My first job was writing content for PhonePe's stockbroking arm. Then Zerodha, where I've been ever since.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="now">
    <h2>What I do now</h2>
    <p>I do research at Zerodha. In practice that means I read, dig and write about whatever is worth understanding, mostly financial services (banking, insurance, broking, wealth, payments) and energy (generation, transmission, new tech). The weirder the rabbit hole, the better. These are three I'm proudest of:</p>
    <div class="picks">
      {homePicks.map((p) => {
        const img = coverFor(p);
        return (
          <a class="card" href={p.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            {img && <img src={img} alt="" width="640" height="427" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />}
            <span class="k">{fmtMonthYear(p.date)}</span>
            <b>{p.title.replace(/, explained$/, '')}</b>
          </a>
        );
      })}
    </div>
    <p>I also help <strong>Rainmatter</strong>, Zerodha's investment arm, with research, and lately that has pulled me deep into climate: the problem statements, the solutions, all of it. That's what keeps me going.</p>
    <p>A lot of what I do is on video too: podcasts, expert interviews on energy and financial services, Varsity videos, and two documentaries, one on the paints war and one on India's race to go green. You'll find them on my <a href="/work/#videos">work page</a>.</p>
    <p>I write on LinkedIn about whatever interests me that week, and sometimes those rabbit holes turn into full research pieces. On the side I built <a href="/finance-radar/">FinanceRadar</a>, a bullshit detector for financial news, because people want good financial content, not noise.</p>
    <p>And quietly, I help a few people sort out their money, one on one and only by referral. Not as a business; I just find it interesting, and I think people deserve good financial advice. I also take career calls with students and give talks whenever someone thinks I have something worth saying. <a href="/financial-planning/">How the money help works →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section id="others">
    <h2>What people tell me</h2>
    <p>I'd rather not describe myself as smart. Here's what I hear instead, from the people I work with and for:</p>
    <div class="says">
      <figure><span class="k">Teammates</span><p>That I give them a sense of direction in research and writing. (A sense I borrowed from people senior to me.)</p></figure>
      <figure><span class="k">Readers</span><p>That the questions I ask are diverse and genuine, and that's what makes the stories worth reading.</p></figure>
      <figure><span class="k">Money-help clients</span><p>That they like the clear intent and clarity of thought I bring.</p></figure>
    </div>
    <p>The one thing friends say most is that I'm passionate about whatever I'm doing. Generic, I know. But if you remember one thing about me, make it this: <span class="hl">I'm really, really inquisitive.</span> Whatever I'm talking about, I get really into it.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="care">
    <h2>What I care about</h2>
    <p>Most people optimise random things. I try to optimise the fundamentals:</p>
    <div class="health">
      <div><span class="k">01</span><b>Financial health</b><small>A simple system that fits your life, and the push to act on it.</small></div>
      <div><span class="k">02</span><b>Physical health</b><small>Cricket, badminton, running, biking, gym, yoga.</small></div>
      <div><span class="k">03</span><b>Mental health</b><small>Staying curious, and open to being wrong.</small></div>
    </div>
    <p>Everything else is noise if these three are broken.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="clock">
    <h2>Off the clock</h2>
    <div class="score">
      {score.map((s) => <div><big>{s.v}{s.u && <small>{s.u}</small>}</big><b>{s.b}</b><span>{s.p}</span></div>)}
    </div>
    <p>Badminton was my sport in school, where I played at the national level. These days it's cricket: Sunday-league tournaments, a few man-of-the-match awards and best-batsman titles. My favourite memory is an 80 in a very competitive match that got personal; it set my team up for a good score.</p>
    <p>I ran a 21K at Nandi Hills completely untrained and loved it, so I know I have a full marathon in me. Maybe an Ironman. Maybe.</p>
    <p>I love biking but don't do it nearly enough. Wayanad and Chikmagalur so far, with the longest ride somewhere around 400 to 500 km. A solo trip around the south is on the list.</p>
    <p>The rest: gym and yoga, travelling when I can, sleeping in whenever I can, tinkering with Claude Code until things work, and an honest amount of procrastinating.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="head">
    <h2>What's in my head</h2>
    <p>The biggest change in me lately: I've become much more tolerant of other viewpoints. I used to think I was smart enough to know everything. Now I've realised there are very few rights and wrongs, and that fascinates me.</p>
    <p>My mental models are borrowed from a lot of places, so it's hard to name one person. But I subscribe to a lot of Naval Ravikant's philosophy, I'm deep into Hinduism and philosophy, and Fight Club is a movie I really like. Beyond that, it honestly depends on what I last consumed. Some weeks I'm obsessed with a writer or a YouTube channel; other weeks I don't remember watching them.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="next">
    <h2>What's next</h2>
    <p>I'm not lost, and I'm not confused. I just want to know what's next for me.</p>
    <p>I think I've set myself up for good things. The questions on my mind right now:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>CFA Level 2 is due.</li>
      <li>Higher education, maybe an MBA. I'm not sure about it yet.</li>
      <li>Get more jacked.</li>
      <li>Learn a new skill or hobby.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section slot="after" class="cell hi span-12">
    <span class="k"><b>●</b>&nbsp; Say hi</span>
    <h2>If you like the vibe, bother me.</h2>
    <p>If any of this interests you, talk to me. A story you think I should chase, something I can help your business with, or just a conversation about any of the above. Nothing gets me going like talking to people who are curious too. I'm most active on LinkedIn.</p>
    <div class="btns">
      <a class="btn" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kashishkap00r" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Message me on LinkedIn</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://x.com/kashishkap00r" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Find me on X</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</LongForm>

<style>
  .ab-av { width: 248px; height: 248px; border-radius: 50%; box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--rule-2), 0 0 0 8px var(--bg), 0 0 0 9px var(--rule); }

  .tee { margin: 26px 0 26px; }
  .tee-bar { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0; background: var(--hi-bg); color: var(--hi-text); padding: 16px; border-radius: 6px 6px 0 0; }
  .tee-bar span { flex: 1 1 30%; padding: 10px 12px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .05em; text-transform: uppercase; border-right: 1px solid rgba(250, 247, 242, .25); }
  .tee-stem { width: 46%; margin: 0 auto; background: var(--hi-bg); color: var(--hi-text); padding: 22px 24px 26px; border-radius: 0 0 6px 6px; }
  .tee-stem .k { color: var(--hi-text); opacity: .75; }
  .tee-stem b { display: block; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 500; font-size: 24px; margin-top: 12px; }
  .tee-stem small { display: block; font-size: 13.5px; opacity: .85; }

  .path { list-style: none !important; padding: 0 !important; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); border-top: 2px solid var(--rule-2); margin: 10px 0 30px !important; }
  .path li { position: relative; padding: 16px 10px 0 0; margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-sans); }
  .path li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; top: -6px; left: 0; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--bg); border: 1.5px solid var(--text-2); }
  .path li:last-child::before { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
  .path b { display: block; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 500; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.25; margin-top: 6px; }
  .path small { display: block; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-2); line-height: 1.4; margin-top: 2px; }

  .picks { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin: 6px 0 26px; }
  .picks .card img { aspect-ratio: 3 / 2; margin: 0 0 10px; border: 0; border-radius: 4px; }
  .picks .card b { display: block; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.3; margin-top: 3px; }
  .picks .card:hover b { color: var(--accent); }

  .says { margin: 6px 0 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .says figure { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr; gap: 16px; padding: 14px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .says figure .k { padding-top: 4px; }
  .says figure p { margin: 0; }

  .health { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6px; margin: 6px 0 20px; }
  .health div { padding: 20px; border-right: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .health div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .health b { display: block; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 500; font-size: 21px; margin: 8px 0 4px; }
  .health small { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-2); line-height: 1.45; display: block; }

  .score { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); margin: 6px 0 24px; }
  .score div { padding: 18px 14px 16px 0; border-right: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-left: 14px; }
  .score div:first-child { padding-left: 0; }
  .score div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .score big { display: block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 38px; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.03em; white-space: nowrap; }
  .score big small { font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); }
  .score b { display: block; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 500; font-size: 18px; margin-top: 10px; }
  .score span { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--text-2); }



  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .ab-av { width: 200px; height: 200px; }
    .tee-bar span { flex-basis: 45%; }
    .tee-stem { width: 70%; }
    .path { grid-template-columns: 1fr; border-top: 0; border-left: 2px solid var(--rule-2); }
    .path li { padding: 0 0 14px 18px; }
    .path li::before { top: 4px; left: -6px; }
    .picks, .health { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .says figure { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
    .health div { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    .score { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .score div { padding-left: 0; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  }
</style>
